From uac5ddd29540c757f at groups.google.com  Mon Jul 10 18:54:05 2017
From: uac5ddd29540c757f at groups.google.com (Linda Molla)
Date: Mon, 10 Jul 2017 18:54:05 +0000
Subject: Calculating coverage of genomic regions
Message-ID: <BI6qy86EjSU.Evgz26AuBAAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/BI6qy86EjSU/m/Evgz26AuBAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I am interested to know if methylkit can be used to find out the coverage of specific regions in the genome. For example of all the potential enhancers or promoters rich in CpGs in a reference genome (example annotated promoters or enhancers in mouse genome)  how many of them are actually well covered through the ERRBS sequencing
If this is not possible through methylkit any recommendations on how to do this using the ERRBS data?

Thank you,
Linda

From uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com  Tue Jul 11 12:30:19 2017
From: uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com (Altuna Akalin)
