In-Reply-To: <BI6qy86EjSU.Evgz26AuBAAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
References: <BI6qy86EjSU.Evgz26AuBAAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/BI6qy86EjSU/m/UmoVzNeFBAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

you can use regionCounts() if you have the locations of the specific regions you are interested in. you can also coerce methylKit objects to GRanges objects and use findOverlaps or subsetByoverlaps from GenomicRanges package.

